-- title:
--   Height-one vertical primes avoid polynomials with non-zero reduction
-- statement:
--   Let $A$ be a discrete valuation ring (a commutative domain which is a discrete valuation ring as a local ring), let $C$ be a commutative domain and an $A$-algebra, and let $x \in C$ be such that the evaluation homomorphism $\mathrm{aeval}\ x \colon A[X] \to C$, $X \mapsto x$, is injective — that is, $x$ is transcendental over $A$ — and such that the underlying ring homomorphism of $\mathrm{aeval}\ x$ is integral, so $C$ is integral over the image $A[x]$. Let $Q \subseteq C$ be a prime ideal whose height equals $1$ and which contains the image under $A \to C$ of the maximal ideal of $A$, in the sense that the ideal generated by that image (the pushforward $\mathfrak m_A \cdot C$) is contained in $Q$. Then for every polynomial $P \in A[X]$ whose coefficientwise reduction modulo $\mathfrak m_A$, i.e. the image of $P$ under the residue map $A \to A/\mathfrak m_A$ applied to coefficients, is non-zero, the element $P(x) = \mathrm{aeval}\ x\ P$ does not lie in $Q$.
--
--   Geometrically the assertion is that a height-one prime of $C$ lying over the closed point of $\operatorname{Spec} A$ must contract, in $A[x] \cong A[X]$, exactly to the generic point $\mathfrak m_A A[X]$ of the special fibre of the $x$-line, so that no polynomial with non-zero reduction can vanish at it. It is used in the study of the integral models of the modular curve $X_1$, both to identify the prime $\mathfrak m_A$ pushed forward along a chart algebra and to analyse the residue fields at height-one primes above $\mathfrak m_A$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_Polynomial_aeval_notMem_of_height_eq_one_of_map_residue_ne_zero.lean

